g gyms  with special instructors who happen to  also be division trainers  advanced firearm classes or technology  courses at local community colleges  again all taught by division experts and  attended by other recruits or active  agents  division agents are expected to maintain  this year-round training for the entire  duration of their service  basic survival skills combat and  intelligence training  is also required to be honed through  regular practice and exercises  the general consensus is that agents are  devoting all spare time  to training and preparation  this group for specialized tactics also  known as the ghosts  is a highly classified elite special  mission unit within the u.s army and  joint special operations command  it is the army's special missions unit  whose members are armed with the state  of the art weapon systems  and are trained in the best field and  combat tactics  they're the most experienced specialised  and qualified special  operations force that the joint special  operations command has to offer  their tactics involve striking enemies  at their most vulnerable  swiftly silently and without being seen  hence the name ghosts  ghost recon teams specialise in covert  operations in politically sensitive  territory with little to no support  typical missions include assassination  or kidnapping of high value targets  to secure or destroy sensitive documents  and classified hardware  and the sabotaging or harassment of key  enemy forces  only the most elite operators are  invited to become ghosts  having already proven themselves in  combat during previous deployments  while all ghosts serve with a strong  sense of honour and duty they understand  that their success will never be  publicly acknowledged by politicians  or public broadcast selection of  potential ghosts is from various  branches of the us military  and they go through a selection phase  which involves a grueling physical  and mental test  although from similar timelines they're  very clearly from different tom clancy  universes  not just because the developers have  said so but also when thinking about  their specific functions  they wouldn't be active at the same time  the division takes place during  and after the collapse of the united  states as well as the rest of the world  they're the last line of defense and are  only activated when all other means have  failed  so in theory the ghosts have already  stood down or been killed in their world  let's assume that the agents and the  ghosts were thrown into an arena  and pit up against each other in a  face-to-face fight  due to the division tech being  considerably more offense orientated i'd  have to say that the agents would come  out on top  but this wouldn't be fair because this  certainly isn't what the ghosts are  intended for  if the two groups were put in a  situation where they had to hunt each  other down  it would be a different story their  training and equipment all focuses on  the ghosts being able to move in  execute and move out without being  noticed  the agents wouldn't see them coming and  they would likely be taken out before  firing a single shot  of course location would be a factor too  the division agents are plucked from  society  tested trained and then put back into  their respective neighborhoods  where they are expected to continue  training for their potential activation  a large part of their preparation is  getting familiar with the environment  where all the vantage points are areas  to avoid getting locked down  and potential safe houses their  activation has them helping their own  communities  where they are in their element while  they both have cutting edge advanced  technology and equipment at their  disposal  they are built for completely different  means  division agents are chosen from all  aspects of life although a lot of come  from the military  not all of them have they're regular  people with normal jobs  they could be first responders 